# What installed copies download from main (raw.githubusercontent.com) is stored byte for byte: release/update.json
# holds the SHA-256 of the launcher, the hooks and the payload, and 1.x reads the launcher as it is (ASCII, CRLF).
# With core.autocrlf, Git would commit these files with other line endings than the ones hashed, and every update
# would be refused. release.py checks that these rules are in place.
/maxpkg-packager.ms -text
/_install.ms -text
/_uninstall.ms -text
/release/** -text
